.TH MKOLD 1 "August 2025" "cvb-tools 0.01" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkold \- timestamped backup/restore helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkold
[\-d DIR] [\-l] [\-r] [\-c [DAYS]] PATH
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkold
creates timestamped backups of files or directories under a base backup directory,
and can restore the latest copy or clear old backups.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-dir DIR
Override base backup directory (default: /var/bkp_files).
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-list
List backups found under the base directory.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-restore
Restore the latest backup for PATH. The current file is first saved with a .res\-TIMESTAMP suffix.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-clear [DAYS]
Delete backups older than DAYS (default 30).
.SH AUTHOR
Andre Machado (cloudvBOX Computing Ltda)
